# Database Rules

Read `docs/05_DATABASE_DESIGN.md` and `docs/06_RBAC.md` before any schema change.

## Naming

- Tables: snake_case plural (`event_participants`)
- Columns: snake_case (`created_at`, `community_id`)
- Enums: snake_case types (`participant_status`)
- Indexes: `idx_{table}_{columns}`
- RPC functions: snake_case verbs (`join_event`)

## Required Columns

All user-facing tables: `id UUID PK`, `created_at`, `updated_at`
Soft-deletable: add `deleted_at TIMESTAMPTZ NULL`
Filter `deleted_at IS NULL` in SELECT policies

## Migrations

- Files in `supabase/migrations/` with timestamp prefix
- One logical change per migration
- Include RLS policies in same migration as table creation
- Never edit applied migrations — create new migration to fix

## RLS

- **Enable RLS on every table** — no exceptions
- Policies documented in `docs/06_RBAC.md`
- Use helper functions: `is_super_admin()`, `is_community_admin()`, `is_community_member()`
- `event_participants`: deny direct INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE — RPC only

## Business Logic in SQL

FCFS join, waitlist, and promotion live in PostgreSQL functions for atomicity.
See `docs/05_DATABASE_DESIGN.md` for function specs.

## Types

Regenerate after migration: `pnpm supabase gen types typescript --local > src/types/database.ts`

## Forbidden

- No court/booking/reservation/slot tables
- No BIGINT serial IDs — UUID only
- No disabling RLS for convenience
